Adds two settings read from the environment at startup:

RIVER_RENDER_BIT_DEPTH=10 renders into XRGB2101010, as sway's
render_bit_depth 10 does, falling back to 8 bits if the output refuses it.

RIVER_DISPLAY_P3_OUTPUTS names outputs whose panel is Display P3. Their
scene output gets sway's --device-primaries transform: the linear sRGB the
scene composites in, mapped to P3 primaries and encoded with the sRGB curve.
That needs the Vulkan renderer; with GLES2 it is logged and skipped.

